ar  promises handle one such event at a time  while  observables handle a sequence of events  over  some time so to give you a brief  explanation promises emit a single value  at a time  while observables are only executed when  subscribed to them using the subscribe  method  now promises also execute immediately  after they are created  and they are not cancelable while  observables help perform operations like  for each  filter retry etc promises  push errors to the child promises and  observables can be unsubscribed to  so that the listener stops receiving  further values  next up what is ng on init and how is it  defined  now again here's a small snippet of code  ng on init is a life cycle hook as we  discussed earlier  and there is a callback method that is  run by angular  to indicate that a component has been  created  it takes no parameters and returns a  void type  so i'm sure you can see here in the code  it takes no parameters and returns a  void  next up explain the use of ng4  in a tag or explain  the ng for director now  the ng for directive is basically  like a for loop it is used to build  lists and tables and html templates so  in  simple terms this directive is used to  iterate over an  array or an object and create template  for each such element  now in the snippet you can see there is  let items in item list  and then i have string interpolated the  variable item so let item here creates a  local variable  that will be available inside the  template of  items indicates that we are iterating  over the items iterable  and the asterisk before ng4 creates a  parent template  next up what are template and reactive  forms so there are two different methods  to create  forms we have the template driven  approach and we have the reactive form  approach  so let's have a look at them in case of  template driven approach  the conventional form tag is used to  create forms  angular automatically interprets and  creates a form object  representation for this tag controls can  be added to the form  using the ng model tag multiple controls  can be  grouped using the ng control group  module  now a form value can be generated using  the form dot value object  and form data is exported as json values  basic html validations can be used to  validate the form fields  in the case of custom validations  directives can be used  when it comes to reactive forms this  approach  basically revolves around data flows and  propagation of change  now with reactive forms the component  directly manages the data flows between  the form controls and the data models  the active forms are code driven unlike  template-driven approach  reactive forms break the traditional  declarative approach  and eliminate the anti-pattern of  updating data via the two-way data  binding method  typically reactive form control creation  is synchronous  and can be unit tested with synchronous  programming techniques  moving on what is bootstrap how is it  added to angular  now bootstrap is a powerful toolkit it  is a collection of  basic html css and javascript tools  for creating and building responsive web  applications  there are two ways to embed bootstrap  libraries  first up is using the bootstrap cdn  which is the content delivery network  now this enables users to load the css  and javascript files  remotely from its servers the other way  is  to use angular bootstrap via npm  now this is used to add bootstrap to  your angular project  by installing it into your project  folder  now you can use commands like npm  install bootstrap  and npm install jquery to install them  for your project  if you wish to learn bootstrap in detail  i highly suggest you check out our video  on  angular bootstrap the tutorial explains  how to embed bootstrap and user to  create and good looking angular  applications  what is eager and lazy loading  eager loading is the default module  loading strategy  now all the feature modules under eager  loading are loaded before your  application even starts  this is typically used for small size  applications since lesser  modules are used all of these modules  are loaded  initially which makes running of these  kind of applications extremely fast when  it comes to lazy loading  all the loading happens dynamically all  feature modules are loaded on demand  it is used for bigger applications where  the modules are not required at the  start of applications  this makes the application faster since  no time is spent on loading unnecessary  modules  next up what type of dom does angular  implement  dom or document object model treats an  xml or html document as a tree structure  in which each node is an object  representing a part of the document  now angular uses the regular dom this  updates the entire tree structure  of html tags until it reaches the data  that has to be updated  now to ensure that the speed and  performance are not affected  angular implements something called as a  change detection  next up how is dependency injection  achieved in angular  now dependencies are objects or services  that a component needs to perform  functions correct now with the help of  dependency injection these classes  can request dependencies from external  sources rather than creating them on  their own  here i've created a service called demo  service using the command  ngg service demo service and i've also  added a small snippet of code when  you create that service  now these services can be injected to  your  main component and perform various  functions  next up how does angular routing work  now i am sure you must have observed  that the url changes  every time you click on your user  interface on an application  correct every time you navigate through  the application or move from one page to  another  the url changes now this means  that the application is being routed or  you're navigating through the  application  so basically routing helps navigate  through a web application  especially in case of single page  applications now as discussed earlier  single page applications are loaded just  once  so any new content that is being  displayed is just a mere  addition it's not being loaded again so  routing plays a vital role in case of  single page applications typically it is  specified with the help of the forward  slash  and followed by a path that defines a  new content  now i'm just taking the same example  that i took before  uh this was the example for string  interpolation however you can see that  we have a navigation bar here  with four different options for that is  home about services and login  and for home and login i've created a  path  and added routing to it so when i click  on the home icon  you can see that some content is being  displayed onto the screen  and if you observe you can see that  there is a forward slash with  the path name home here which indicates  that routing has occurred  same with login when i click on it the  path changes  and the login page appears if you wish  to learn  the concept of routing i suggest you  check out a video  the tutorial explains routing in detail  moving on what are form control and form  groups  now a form control is basically a class  that enables validation  for each input field an instance of this  class is created  and these instances help check the  values of the field  and see if they are touched untouched  dirty pristine  valid invalid and so on so for every  field  in the form the data that is being  provided is validated with the help of  these controls  if it is dirty it means that the value  has been changed  if the data provided holds good for a  particular condition  then the control is set to be valid  and so on with the help of these  controls you can determine if the value  provided is legitimate or not  this can be achieved with the help of  form control  when it comes to form group and the form  group class represents a group of  controls  number form can have multiple control  groups  the form group class returns true if all  the controls are valid  and also provides validation errors if  any  next up is how is testing achieved in  angular  now angular uses jasmine to run various  tests  the jasmine framework allows various  functionalities  to write different kinds of test cases  the task runner for these tests is  typically  karma and karma uses a configuration  file  to set the startup reporters and the  testing framework  next question is what is package.json  now npm installs package.json when a new  workspace is created  now this file includes a starter set of  packages  some of which are required by angular  now typically it's organized into two  groups one is  dependencies these are essential to run  your applications  and we have dev dependencies these are  essential to develop  applications so with that we come to the  end of this video  i hope it helped you get a good hold of  angular fundamentals  if you have any doubts or queries let us  know in the comment section below  thank you so much for being here and  watch out for more videos from us  until then keep learning and stay tuned  to simply learn  hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simply learn youtube  channel  and click here to watch similar videos  turn it up and get certified  click here

